-- title:
--   Two-chart gluing data of a line bundle trivial modulo a nilpotent ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $J \subseteq A$ an ideal that is nilpotent, let $X$ be a scheme with a morphism $c \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, and let $\mathcal{V}$ be a two-affine open cover of $X$, that is, two opens $U_0, U_1 \subseteq X$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ such that $U_0$, $U_1$ and $U_0 \sqcap U_1$ are affine. Write $A_0 = \Gamma(X, U_0)$, $A_1 = \Gamma(X, U_1)$, $A_{01} = \Gamma(X, U_0 \sqcap U_1)$, regarded as $A$-algebras through $c$, and $\rho_0, \rho_1$ for the restriction $A$-algebra maps into $A_{01}$. Let $L$ be a sheaf of modules on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ for which the pullback of $L$ along $U \hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit module on $U$, and assume that the pullback of $L$ along the first projection $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec}(A/J) \to X$ is isomorphic to the unit module on that fibre product. Then there exist an element $a$ of $A_{01}$ lying in the ideal generated by the image of $J$, together with an $A_0$-linear isomorphism $e_0 \colon \Gamma(L, U_0) \cong A_0$, an $A_1$-linear isomorphism $e_1 \colon \Gamma(L, U_1) \cong A_1$ and an $A_{01}$-linear isomorphism $e_{01} \colon \Gamma(L, U_0 \sqcap U_1) \cong A_{01}$, such that $e_{01}(x|_{U_0 \sqcap U_1}) = \rho_0(e_0(x))$ for every section $x$ over $U_0$ and $e_{01}(y|_{U_0 \sqcap U_1}) = (1+a)\,\rho_1(e_1(y))$ for every section $y$ over $U_1$.
--
--   This is the two-chart Čech form of the description of the kernel of $\operatorname{Pic}(X) \to \operatorname{Pic}(X_0)$ for the thickening of $X$ defined by a nilpotent ideal of the base: a line bundle trivial on $X_0$ is trivial on each chart and is glued by a transition unit of the shape $1 + a$ with $a \in J A_{01}$. It is used in the analysis of the relative Picard functor, where it feeds the comparison of deformations trivial modulo $J$ with the first Čech cohomology of the ideal sheaf.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_Modules_IsInvertible_exists_sectionsOf_equiv_lineBundle_one_add_of_pullback_quotient_isNilpotent.lean

